Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-09-2001||12:04 PM||||My car has terrible orange peel onthe paint.. is there anything I can do to get it o shine without a new paintjob? thanks@!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR>  pics are coming :)||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||11-09-2001||06:22 PM||||You could try to wet sand and polish it. This would smooth out the paint. The only problem is if you go to far you will take the clear coat off and then you will have to get the car painted. Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mgbringo||11-09-2001||09:44 PM||||Is it base coat/clear coat or enamel or laquer?<P>I agree the best way is to color sand it with 1,000 and then 1,500, and then 2,000 wet sand paper and then buff it out with some polishing compound.<P>Lots of work but you can get it like glass with enough elbow grease.||||reg||1
